  - IP: 192.168.10.50
- [x] Installed Wazuh manager and dashboard
- [x] Created custom admin account (changed default credentials)
- [x] Dashboard accessible at https://192.168.10.50:443
- **Time:** ~45 minutes

**Part 3: Agent Enrollment**
- [x] Deployed Wazuh agent on Proxmox host (192.168.10.5)
  - Downloaded latest agent from Wazuh repo
  - Configured <client> section with manager IP and port 1514
  - Verified service running and active
- [x] Deployed Wazuh agent on Windows 11 desktop
  - Same installation and configuration process
  - Both agents showed **Active** in dashboard within 60 seconds
- **Time:** ~20 minutes

**Part 4: First Detection Test**
- [x] Generated SSH login failures (5 attempts with wrong credentials)
- [x] Observed real-time alerts in Wazuh dashboard
- [x] Captured screenshots of:
  - Active agents (Management → Agents)
  - SSH failure events (Monitoring → Events)
- [x] Verified full detection pipeline: event → capture → ingest → display
- **Time:** ~15 minutes

### Lessons Learned
1. Always reference official vendor documentation (Wazuh docs, not third-party guides)
2. Version numbers matter (4.x vs 5.x in repository URLs)
3. `apt install` for .deb packages handles dependencies better than `dpkg`
4. Agent config typos cause silent failures — double-check `<client>` IP/port
5. Agents take ~60 seconds to appear in dashboard after starting
6. Browser performance can lag when Wazuh processes first agent logs (normal)

